{
  "_comment": [
    "Estimated request costs for the pi-request-stats extension.",
    "Rates are per 1,000,000 tokens, in USD, read from the Standard / Batch / Flex / Fast / Ultrafast",
    "tables at https://developers.openai.com/api/docs/pricing on 2026-10-18. Update the numbers when",
    "OpenAI changes them.",
    "Each mode carries its long-context rates in \"tiers\": they apply to a request once its input tokens",
    "(input + cache read + cache write) exceed aboveTokens — 272,000 for these models, the same threshold",
    "pi's own model catalog uses. A \"long\" / \"longContext\" block sitting beside flat rates, or a",
    "top-level \"tiers\" array, is read as a tier of the standard mode rather than as a price mode.",
    "Cache writes are 125% of the input rate; models the page omits from a table have no such mode",
    "(GPT-6 Luna has no Ultrafast prices).",
    "Add your own models or override these in ~/.pi/agent/pi-request-stats.pricing.json or .pi/pi-request-stats.pricing.json",
    "(later files win, model by model). An entry may list extra ids that share its prices:",
    "\"aliases\": [\"my-local-model\"], or map one id onto another entry with \"my-id\": \"gpt-6.1-sol\".",
    "Accepted field spellings: input; cachedInput | cacheRead | cachedInputTokens | cache;",
    "cacheWrite | writeOutputTokens; cacheWrite1h (1-hour prompt-cache writes, charged at 2x base input",
    "when no rate is given, like pi does); output | reasoningOutputTokens.",
    "Set \"fallbackModel\": \"\" to stop pricing models that have no entry here.",
    "Turn cost estimation off entirely with \"cost\": false in any of those files (or PI_REQUEST_STATS_COST=off,",
    "PI_REQUEST_STATS_NO_COST=1, --pi-request-stats-no-cost, /cost off). With it off nothing is priced, so the status bar",
    "drops the money readout and no \"add prices for this model\" hint appears; /cost on switches it back.",
    "Set the flag to \"on\"/\"off\" or true/false; env and command settings win over the files."
  ],
  "currency": "USD",
  "perTokens": 1000000,
  "mode": "standard",
  "preferReportedCost": true,
  "multiplier": 1,
  "fallbackModel": "gpt-6.1-sol",
